hello and welcome again to a tutorial on  a new competition that we have recently  published  this time we are selecting heads of  administration in eu delegations  a delegation is kind of an embassy of  the eu in a third country so not in an  eu member state but in a country outside  of the eu  we have as usual published an  infographic on our website which shows  you in a blink of an eye the eligibility  criteria and the different stages of the  competition  and in this tutorial i will give you  some more in-depth information on these  different stages  of the competition  when it comes to eligibility this  competition is published on great ast 4  which basically means that either you  need  post-secondary education and six years  of experience in the field  or secondary education and nine years of  experience in the field  when i say in the field it has to be a  field which is listed below one of the  fields listed below and there's quite a  choice for this competition  so your degree and your experience  should be in either law  hr  accounting engineering business  administration  finance logistics or building management  you have quite a choice here  to choose from then there's also a  language criterium of course your first  language can be any of the 24 official  languages  your second language must be either  english or french  now  personally i think it's quite an  exciting position i'd like to compare  these heads of administration with a  swiss knife they are  multi-tools you know they are also  multitasking heads of administration run  the day-to-day business of a delegation  so they are involved in hr matters in  project management in security in  building management  so they are they have really kind of an  extensive portfolio  to take care of  the selection procedure is quite  standardized as you may have seen in  previous  tutorials so once you have applied  you are invited to a first stage of  testing  where we test your reasoning skills  second stage is a talent screener i will  explain in a minute what that entails  the last stage is an assessment center  where we test a set of competencies  the successful candidates are listed on  a reserve list of successful candidates  and those are the ones that then will be  recruited  into these delegations  so let's have a closer look at these  different stages  application of course starts with an  epso account if you do not have an exo  account yet you can easily create one if  you do have one use that account to  apply do not create a new account  because you can only have one account  you only need one account for all your  applications with eu careers  you can only apply online on our website  obviously and you have to apply  or you can apply in any of the 24  languages  apart from the talent screener part  which you have to fill in english i will  explain in a minute what this is  you should validate your application by  the 27th of september so you have quite  some time to do so  you don't have to apply in one go you  can start your application save your  your entries and then come back at a  later stage just make sure that you  validate your application at the latest  on the 27th of september  everybody who applies will be invited to  the first stage of testing which is a  test where we test your reasoning skills  we test your verbal numerical and  abstract reasoning skills  in your language one  you see the number of questions we we  ask you you see the duration you get to  solve these questions  you need a combined pass mark of at  least 20 out of 40  combined meaning that you could  fail for one of these tests as long as  you make up for your  scoring in the other tests you need at  least 20 out of 40.  i do strongly advise you to train this  and you can do so by having a look at  our sample tests which are available on  our website  you can test this in any of the 24  languages  and by doing so you will get better at  this because first of all there is the  level of difficulty of these questions  but there's also this time factor  involved and by rehearsing this by  practicing this you will get better at  this and you will  improve  if you pass this stage you will be  invited to the second stage  which is the talent screener phase  you yourself you don't have to do  anything anymore because you have filled  this  face when you applied  so what happens now is that the  selection board will check your answers  to the questions in this talent screener  the talent screener is a set of 10  questions where we assess your  professional experience in these  different fields you know the different  aspects of the job of a head of  administration  the selection board will rank  all the candidates  through the answers given by the  candidates and the best ones ranked will  be invited to the third stage of testing  which is the assessment center  first we test a set of general  competencies seven of them you see them  listed on this slide here  and we do so by  having the candidates sit two different  tests  the case study which is a written  exercise will test four competencies  and the situational competency based  interview will test three more  competencies okay  again you need a combined pass mark of  35 out of 70 you get  maximum 10 points per competency and you  need at least 35  all over  then of course we also test your field  related competencies and this is done by  a field related interview so again an  interview with the selection board  which you sit again in french or english  by the way your general competencies are  also tested in your second language  english or french  for the field related competency tests  you need also at least 50 out of 100s  and the score combined  general competencies and field direct  competencies will give you the final  mark  and the best ranked people will be the  ones who are the successful candidates  we're looking to select 40 successful  candidates and these are the ones that  then will be offered the job in these  delegations  please do read the notice of competition  carefully the notice of competition is a  legal document explaining the whole  competition the duties the eligibility  criteria the different steps of the  competition explained in detail again so  please  read this document carefully if you  would still have questions after that  you can of course always reach out to us  through the web form on our website and  we of course will be happy to answer all  your queries  i hope this was useful please do apply  and hopefully you can join us later on  as one of our successful recently  recruited heads of administration in a  delegation thanks for your attention and  see you next time bye
 

